---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import ContentSection from "../components/ContentSection.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Pilgrimage Homeschool Science Olympiad">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <h1>Pilgrimage Homeschool</h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">
      A competitive Science Olympiad team for homeschooled students in Maryland.
    </p>

    <div class="button-group">
      <Button href="/about/" label="Learn About Us" />
      <Button href="/contact/" label="Contact Us" variant="secondary" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContentSection title="About Us">
    <p>
      Pilgrimage Homeschool Science Olymipad Team is the only non
      school-affiliated team of over 70 schools competing in Maryland.
      Pilgrimage has been highly competitive since 2010, coming 1st in the state
      of Maryland four times to represent Maryland at the national tournament.
      Our Division B or Middle School team has never placed under the top 5 of
      30 in the state tournament.
    </p>
  </ContentSection>

  <section class="page-section">
    <h2>About Science Olympiad</h2>
    <p>
      In Science Olympiad, students compete in events, which are essentially
      tests of their knowledge in many different scientific areas. There are
      three types of events:
    </p>
<div class="event-grid">
  <article class="info-card">
    <h3>Study Events</h3>
    <p>
      Composed of a subject test (e.g., Meteorology).
    </p>
  </article>

  <article class="info-card">
    <h3>Build Events</h3>
    <p>
      Require students to create a scientific device (e.g., Tower).
    </p>
  </article>

  <article class="info-card">
    <h3>Lab Events</h3>
    <p>
      Consist of a test and hands-on analysis portion (e.g., Forensics).
    </p>
  </article>
</div>
</section>

  <ContentSection title="Past Successes" variant="achievement">
    <p>
      In April 2024, Pilgrimage Homeschool competed at the Maryland State Tournament for Divisions A, B & C, also known as Elementary, Middle and High School. Pilgrimage's elementary school team rose from 2nd place in 2023 to 1st place in 2024! Our middle school team earned the 4th place spot in the state!  
    </p>
  </ContentSection>
</BaseLayout>
